From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 0098] 0098: leave the physmap dead zone - pram mapping after
 the TTBR1 switch, aperture block dropped

QEMU r32 (5cdce86) faulted at arm_vm_init+0xbe4: the 0097 aperture block
called phystokv() after arm_vm_physmap_init() had populated ptov_table but
before set_mmu_ttb_alternate() switched TTBR1 to the final tables.  In that
window phystokv returns a slid physmap-window VA that exists only in the
not-yet-live final tables (bootstrap TTBR1 has no L1 entry for it), so the
first access dies with an L1 translation fault.  r31 died the same way at
_bzero+0x1c (the 0096 pram block's own bzero of alloc_ptpage's VA).

Measured ground truth (QEMU pmemsave + payload symtab):
 - ptov_table at that point: [rest-of-physmem pa=0x1024d0000], [gPhysBase];
 - physmap window = L1 slot 2015 of cpu_tte, L2 entries 26..152 populated;
 - bootstrap TTBR1 lacks that L1 slot entirely until the switch;
 - nothing in the tree touches VM_MIN+32MB ("slot 1 hole" was the r31
   misdiagnosis - the faulting PC was the pram block's bzero, not
   map_final).

Fix: drop the aperture block; run the pram mapping after set_mmu_ttb_
alternate() where the physmap aperture is live.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
index 6c41a5a..e8e02b3 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
@@ -2214,37 +2214,19 @@ arm_vm_init(uint64_t memory_size, boot_args * args)
 	sweet_early_map_final();
 #endif
 	arm_vm_physmap_init(args);
-#if defined(SWEET)
-	/* The bootstrap aperture VAs (phystokv of the PT pages, the ADT and
-	 * boot_args at pa 0x102xxxxxx) live in L2 slot 1 of the kernel's own
-	 * L1 slot.  The pre-switch identity covered them, but the final
-	 * tables never did - the old fb alias happened to occupy that slot
-	 * and mask the hole.  Map the window as a Normal-cacheable 32MB
-	 * block BEFORE the TTBR1 switch (the write itself needs TTBR0):
-	 * post-switch accesses (pmap_enter_bootstrap's table writes, the
-	 * pram mapping, kvtophys) all go through these VAs. */
-	{
-		vm_map_address_t ap_va = (vm_map_address_t)0xfffffe0020000000ULL;
-		pmap_paddr_t ap_pa = gPhysBase + 0x2000000ULL;
-		tt_entry_t *l1_tte = cpu_tte + ((ap_va & ARM_TT_L1_INDEX_MASK) >> ARM_TT_L1_SHIFT);
-		tt_entry_t *l2t = (tt_entry_t *)phystokv(*l1_tte & ARM_TTE_TABLE_MASK);
-		tt_entry_t *l2_tte = l2t + ((ap_va & ARM_TT_L2_INDEX_MASK) >> ARM_TT_L2_SHIFT);
-
-		assert(*l2_tte == ARM_TTE_EMPTY);
-		*l2_tte = ap_pa | ARM_TTE_VALID | ARM_TTE_TYPE_BLOCK |
-		    ARM_TTE_BLOCK_SH(SH_OUTER_MEMORY) |
-		    ARM_TTE_BLOCK_ATTRINDX(CACHE_ATTRINDX_DEFAULT) |
-		    ARM_TTE_BLOCK_AF;
-		__asm__ volatile("dsb ishst" ::: "memory");
-	}
-#endif
+	set_mmu_ttb_alternate(cpu_ttep & TTBR_BADDR_MASK);
 #if defined(SWEET)
 	/* The panic region (pram) sits immediately above real_avail_end,
 	 * outside the physmap aperture and outside phystokv's range, and
-	 * check_for_panic_log's ml_io_map runs in the bootstrap-era tables
-	 * that do not survive the TTBR1 switch (PE_init_panicheader faulted
-	 * on platina: boot #25 QEMU nested panic).  Map it by hand at a
-	 * fixed VA in a free L1 slot of the final tables. */
+	 * check_for_panic_log's ml_io_map runs too late to help
+	 * (PE_init_panicheader faulted on platina: boot #25 QEMU nested
+	 * panic).  Map it by hand at a fixed VA in a free L1 slot of the
+	 * final tables.  This MUST run after the TTBR1 switch: pre-switch
+	 * alloc_ptpage's phystokv resolves through the slid physmap window,
+	 * which the still-running bootstrap tables do not map (QEMU r31:
+	 * bzero fault at _bzero+0x1c; r32: the same class at
+	 * arm_vm_init+0xbe4).  Post-switch cpu_tte's physmap L1/L2 carry
+	 * the window, so phystokv works normally here. */
 	{
 		vm_map_address_t pram_va = (vm_map_address_t)0xfffffe0105dc0000ULL;
 		pmap_paddr_t pram_pa = args->physBase + args->memSize;
@@ -2265,7 +2247,6 @@ arm_vm_init(uint64_t memory_size, boot_args * args)
 		sweet_pram_va = pram_va;
 	}
 #endif
-	set_mmu_ttb_alternate(cpu_ttep & TTBR_BADDR_MASK);
 
 	ml_enable_monitor();
 
